   "html_text": "While the orthodoxy of truth-conditional accounts of meaning adds weight to the view that this putative conflict poses a challenge to deflationism, it is still, contra Devitt, an open question whether any non-truth-conditional account of meaning will turn out to be adequate and to supersede truth-conditional semantics. Moreover, even if there is no viable “truth-free” account, several philosophers (e.g., Bar-on, et al. 2005) have argued that deflationism has no more problem with a truth-conditio",
